  "knownDifferences": [
    "GeoMoose 3.15.2 adds neither OpenGeo bearer nor selected-organization headers to these direct sources. The exact modules and representations interoperate, but private use requires authenticated host mediation; a separately governed anonymous publication is not introduced here.",
    "The ArcGIS facade is a bounded read adapter over one immutable OpenGeo service binding: envelope intersection, IDs, one feature batch, and one raster export. It is not an ArcGIS Server implementation and does not support edits, arbitrary where clauses, statistics, pagination, or service administration.",
    "GeoMoose's ags-vector source requires JSONP. OpenGeo admits only a bounded JavaScript identifier callback, rejects duplicate and unknown parameters, and retains private no-store policy; configured-origin deployment behavior remains unverified.",
    "The exact client run is local and network-free. Governed public/private publication, CORS/TLS, live authentication, deployment, withdrawal races, load, devices, rollback, and billing remain separate evidence."
  ]
